# Per-destination allowlist (Doc 04 SEC-03) — one regex per line, matched
# against destination hosts. DEV VALUES: the mock channel services plus MinIO
# (test fixtures serve media bytes from the object store; the fake adapter is a
# code fixture with no host of its own). Production values are real channel API
# hosts only — Doc 18 owns that wiring (ADR 0008).
#
# NOT on this list, deliberately: mailpit (the SEC-03 test fetches from it to
# prove the deny), postgres, redis — an SSRF that can reach the data layer is
# the exact attack this file exists to stop.
^mock-telegram$
^mock-sms$
^mock-ai$
^minio$
# Doc 05 (Telegram Channel): the first REAL channel API. Added by config per
# ADR 0008 — all Bot API traffic (getMe, setWebhook, sendMessage, getFile)
# goes through this proxy; a direct call to api.telegram.org is a violation.
^api\.telegram\.org$
# Doc 09 (S09 step 5, ADR 0016/0019): the AI provider host — every LLM call
# rides this proxy; the fixtures-only guard polices WHAT leaves, this file
# polices WHERE it may go.
^api\.addisassistant\.com$
# Doc 14 (S14 step 4, R-D14-1.6, ADR 0008): the GeezSMS aggregator — the gateway of record; every
# send rides this proxy (the mock-sms FIXTURE stands in locally; a live call needs a vault-held token).
^api\.geezsms\.com$
